cluster. Before the promotion the standby compares its own timeline and
WAL replay position with the peer's and refuses to promote if the peer is
ahead, so that a stale node cannot win after a staggered shutdown of both
nodes. If the peer does not answer within this time the standby is
promoted anyway (availability) and a warning with both known states is
logged. While the peer's position still advances (crash recovery) the wait
is extended up to a fixed limit of 100 seconds, which stays below the
default promote timeout of 120 seconds.

